WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.105 --> 00:00:07.268
That must be them there
near that big piece of nothing.

2
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:09.070
<i>According to my G.P. S...</i>

3
00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:11.304
it's about where Texas turns into Oklahoma.

4
00:00:11.413 --> 00:00:15.679
Oh. great. Right in the middle
of a jurisdictional pissing contest.

5
00:00:17.185 --> 00:00:19.551
Look. I'm out of water. Give me yours.

6
00:00:19.654 --> 00:00:21.121
Hey!

7
00:00:22.324 --> 00:00:25.122
Hey! Are y'all F.B. I?

8
00:00:25.226 --> 00:00:27.194
F.B.I. Special Agent Seeley Booth.

9
00:00:27.295 --> 00:00:30.196
This here is Dr. Temperance Brennan
from theJeffersonian.

10
00:00:30.298 --> 00:00:33.461
<i>- Welcome to Oklahoma. ma'am.
- Welcome to Texas. ma'am.</i>

11
00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:35.229
Guys. welcome
to the United States of America.

12
00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:37.532
- Where are the remains. please?
- Oh!

13
00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:40.039
Right here.

14
00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:46.174
<i>Hardly any flesh left.</i>

15
00:00:46.281 --> 00:00:48.249
<i>It's very dry here...</i>

16
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.977
<i>so I'm guessing that time of death
was some months ago.</i>

17
00:00:51.085 --> 00:00:55.681
- How do you think they died?
- They left Oklahoma. hit Texas. then died of despair.

18
00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.622
Nope. They're definitely Oklahomans.

19
00:00:58.726 --> 00:01:01.058
If they were from Texas.
they'd have had sense enough to carry water.

20
00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:03.527
That wouldn't show up in the bones.

21
00:01:03.631 --> 00:01:06.191
<i>- No clothing.
- Might've blown away.</i>

22
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.791
<i>Maybe a young couple.
some kind of suicide pact?</i>

23
00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.894
<i>Sub-pubic angle suggests two females.</i>

24
00:01:12.006 --> 00:01:15.339
- Oh! Lesbian suicide pact.
- Definitely Texans then.

25
00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:19.242
<i>The victims were pygopagus
or. some would say. illeopagus.</i>

26
00:01:19.346 --> 00:01:21.906
- What's that? - Greek?
- Conjoined twins.

27
00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:23.984
- What's that?
- Siamese twins.

28
00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.552
<i>The point of attachment is posterior.</i>

29
00:01:26.654 --> 00:01:29.919
- Ah. joined at the ass.
- Definitely Texans.

30
00:01:30.024 --> 00:01:32.083
<i>So what do we got here. Doc?</i>

31
00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.820
Well. it's a federal case. boys.
F.B.I. will take jurisdiction.

32
00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:44.671
Conjoined twin births
occur once every 85.000 births...

33
00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:47.240
the same frequency as hermaphroditic births.

34
00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:51.004
<i>Oh. Mr. Nigel-Murray.
we've so missed your insights.</i>

35
00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:54.478
- Thank you.
- Why weren't the remains dispersed by scavengers?

36
00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.549
Well. the depression
in the earth suggested...

37
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.551
that they were buried
in an extremely shallow grave.

38
00:01:59.653 --> 00:02:02.053
The remains were spotted
by an oil survey team from a helicopter.

39
00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:04.590
Begging the question. what exposed the bones?

40
00:02:04.692 --> 00:02:08.219
<i>Well. there was a sandstorm
in that area eight days ago.</i>

41
00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.297
<i>Sustained winds of 60 miles an hour.
gusts of about 80.</i>

42
00:02:11.398 --> 00:02:14.799
Third molars have not completely emerged.
and root development is incomplete.

43
00:02:14.902 --> 00:02:18.894
<i>Indicating that the victims
were between 19 and 21 years of age.</i>

44
00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.964
Guys. hello.
I.D.'ing them is not going to be a problem.

45
00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.203
How many sets of conjoined twins
can there be?

46
00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.872
<i>Um. over the last 500 years.
approximately 600 sets...</i>

47
00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.472
<i>over 70 percent women.</i>

48
00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.052
I did not expect him to know that.

49
00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.919
<i>Well. all facts are useful.
It's just the context that shifts.</i>

50
00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:41.016
<i>I bet I couldjust go search
for missing Siamese twins...</i>

51
00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.061
and find them in. like. 10 minutes.

52
00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:48.065
- By all means. give it a shot.
- The victims have two separate spinal columns...

53
00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:51.432
fused distally at the lower sacral level.
extending to the pelvis.

54
00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:53.505
No other vertebral anomalies.

55
00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.972
Neither one of them could've survived
the death of the other.

56
00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.806
So murder/suicide.
suicide/murder or vice versa.

57
00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.142
That was vice versa.

58
00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:06.116
<i>Soil beneath the skeletons was full of weirdness.</i>

59
00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.187
Quite a bit of decomposed cotton.

60
00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:11.279
- We didn't see any fabric.
- Wow. It was decomposed.

61
00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.257
It was fairly cheap stuff too.
I think they were wrapped in a sheet.

62
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.385
Naked. wrapped in a sheet.

63
00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.464
Sweets will have something to say about that.

64
00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.761
<i>Also. I found soil-dwelling mites-
genus Ameronothrus.</i>

65
00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.632
<i>Nearest place they could've picked up
soil mites was hundreds of miles away.</i>

66
00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.297
And decomposed popcorn.

67
00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.499
They were killed at the movies?

68
00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.839
- I have a theory-
- The circus.

69
00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.971
<i>Kind of stole my thunder there.</i>

70
00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.811
<i>But yeah. Yeah. The traveling circus.</i>

71
00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:42.184
- I found them.
- Already?

72
00:03:46.925 --> 00:03:48.893
- Huh? The circus.
- The circus.

73
00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.325
- The circus.
- The circus.

74
00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.696
"Abracadabra" was first uttered
to cure hay fever.

75
00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:01.196
Conjoined twins wrapped in a sheet?

76
00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:03.206
- Yep.
- According to Hodgins.

77
00:04:03.308 --> 00:04:05.208
It would help to know
how they were wrapped.

78
00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.005
All the evidence is gone with the wind.

79
00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:09.012
- No other clothing?
- According to Hodgins.

80
00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:11.708
<i>The murderer didn't want anyone
to identify them from their clothes.</i>

81
00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.717
They're conjoined twins.

82
00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:17.585
You might as well have buried them
with their driver's licenses in their hands.

83
00:04:17.689 --> 00:04:21.989
Wrapped naked bodies often indicate
a careful burial or. of course. sexual assault.

84
00:04:22.093 --> 00:04:24.994
Okay. you know what? That's. uh-
That's creepy. We gotta get going. Sweets.

85
00:04:25.096 --> 00:04:27.030
<i>- Where?
- Texas. That's where the circus is.</i>

86
00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:31.364
Uh. circus folk are extremely
tight-lipped and close-knit.

87
00:04:31.469 --> 00:04:33.437
They won't tell you anything.

88
00:04:33.538 --> 00:04:38.339
- How do you know?
- I-You know. I've read articles.

89
00:04:38.443 --> 00:04:41.003
You're the worst liar I have ever met.
You read articles?

90
00:04:41.112 --> 00:04:43.910
- Even I know he's lying.
- Okay. I'm adopted.

91
00:04:44.015 --> 00:04:46.006
You know-You know what?
My story isn't important here.

92
00:04:46.117 --> 00:04:48.278
No. it's very important. Go ahead.

93
00:04:48.386 --> 00:04:52.015
I-
When I reached the age of majority...

94
00:04:52.123 --> 00:04:54.683
I tried to find my birth mother-

95
00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:59.423
a psychic who worked
the circus-and-carnival circuit in Florida.

96
00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:02.989
- Bio mom was a carny.
- You know what? Let's stay on track.

97
00:05:03.101 --> 00:05:05.399
The point is. no one would talk to me.

98
00:05:05.503 --> 00:05:07.596
- Were you wearing a suit?
- You'll be wearing a suit.

99
00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:10.869
And they won't open up to you either.
I'm just trying to be helpful here.

100
00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:12.910
I suspect Sweets is right.

101
00:05:13.011 --> 00:05:15.308
I studied a carnival for six weeks...

102
00:05:15.412 --> 00:05:18.040
as research
for my cultural anthropology dissertation.

103
00:05:18.148 --> 00:05:20.116
No one would tell me anything...

104
00:05:20.217 --> 00:05:22.378
even though I became
quite adept on the high wire.

105
00:05:22.486 --> 00:05:26.422
Fine. If they're gonna talk to their own.
we will go undercover.

106
00:05:26.523 --> 00:05:29.117
- What?
- If we're joining a circus. we'll need an act.

107
00:05:29.226 --> 00:05:31.820
- I'm quite adept on the high wire.
- No. no. no. You know what?

108
00:05:31.929 --> 00:05:34.159
- We'll have a knife-throwing act.
- Well. I can't throw knives.

109
00:05:34.265 --> 00:05:36.825
<i>I can. I had the best knife skills
in the Rangers.</i>

110
00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:40.165
Are we going to join the circus?

111
00:05:40.271 --> 00:05:42.899
We are gonna join the circus.

112
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:50.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

113
00:06:18.575 --> 00:06:22.534
<i>We're gonna talk to the twins'mother here
in Fort Worth. then pick up our mobile home.</i>

114
00:06:22.646 --> 00:06:25.843
- And we'll join the circus right outside Waco.
- Uh. our mobile home?

115
00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.941
Yeah. We're circus folks. Bones.

116
00:06:28.052 --> 00:06:30.885
We crisscross the country in a mobile home.

117
00:06:30.988 --> 00:06:33.422
I had the field office here
paint up something special for us.

118
00:06:33.524 --> 00:06:36.516
Is that all you need
to get a job at the circus- a mobile home?

119
00:06:36.627 --> 00:06:40.563
You know what? It's gonna help.
It's showy. And we're show people.

120
00:06:40.664 --> 00:06:43.427
It's always possible that we'll
talk to the girls' mother...

121
00:06:43.533 --> 00:06:45.865
and solve this whole case tonight.

122
00:06:45.969 --> 00:06:48.028
- Right?
- I hope not.

123
00:06:48.137 --> 00:06:50.697
- What? Huh?
- Hmm?

124
00:06:58.915 --> 00:07:02.476
<i>I should've never let those girls leave this home.</i>

125
00:07:02.585 --> 00:07:04.576
Worst thing that can happen
to a mother. isn't it?

126
00:07:04.687 --> 00:07:09.386
Finding out that you outlived your child.
Unnatural.

127
00:07:09.492 --> 00:07:11.722
Except for societies
with high infant mortality rates.

128
00:07:11.828 --> 00:07:15.059
<i>My understanding is you tried to sue
the circus several times. Mrs. Van Owen.</i>

129
00:07:15.164 --> 00:07:19.567
- It's Mrs. Hicks.
- Dell Hicks here is my husband and my lawyer.

130
00:07:19.669 --> 00:07:22.001
Dell helped me sue the circus for-

131
00:07:22.105 --> 00:07:24.505
Loss of income. alienation of affection...

132
00:07:24.607 --> 00:07:28.600
<i>civil rights abuses.
animal abuses. improper hiring...</i>

133
00:07:28.711 --> 00:07:30.702
emotional distress. mental anguish.

134
00:07:30.813 --> 00:07:34.078
- Any of these go to court?
- It's just a matter of time. Agent Booth.

135
00:07:34.183 --> 00:07:36.208
Hmm. You really hated that circus.

136
00:07:36.319 --> 00:07:40.551
They stole my daughters.
I'll do anything to get back at them for that.

137
00:07:40.656 --> 00:07:43.784
<i>- When did you last see your daughters?
- Four months ago.</i>

138
00:07:43.893 --> 00:07:46.885
- They told us to butt out of their lives.
- Jenny did.

139
00:07:46.996 --> 00:07:48.964
If one of the girls wanted something...

140
00:07:49.065 --> 00:07:51.363
it was the same as both of'em wanting it.

141
00:07:51.467 --> 00:07:53.492
IfJenny wanted something.
then they both wanted it.

142
00:07:53.603 --> 00:07:56.401
Didn't matter whatJulie wanted.

143
00:07:56.506 --> 00:07:58.633
<i>I took a look at the remains...</i>

144
00:07:58.741 --> 00:08:03.007
and I had to wonder if you ever considered
having them surgically separated.

145
00:08:03.112 --> 00:08:05.239
It was too dangerous.

146
00:08:05.348 --> 00:08:08.408
- I disagree.
- So did Jenny and Dr. Muir.

147
00:08:08.518 --> 00:08:12.613
Well. Julie and I thought
it was too dangerous.

148
00:08:12.721 --> 00:08:16.657
Your daughters disagreed
on whether or not they should be separated?

149
00:08:18.193 --> 00:08:20.491
Dr. Muir's office- here in Forth Worth?

150
00:08:22.431 --> 00:08:26.959
I'm sure you understand that my responses
to your questions about the Van Owen sisters...

151
00:08:27.069 --> 00:08:29.435
is somewhat tempered by patient privilege.

152
00:08:29.538 --> 00:08:31.438
They're murder victims. right?

153
00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:33.440
Patient privilege no longer applies.

154
00:08:33.542 --> 00:08:36.636
Well. yes. of course.

155
00:08:36.745 --> 00:08:39.646
I've never- I've never had
a patient murdered before.

156
00:08:39.748 --> 00:08:43.343
<i>You thought that the twins
could safely be separated?</i>

157
00:08:43.452 --> 00:08:45.420
- Yes.
- I agree.

158
00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:49.581
As did Jenny.
ButJulie and her mother disagreed.

159
00:08:49.691 --> 00:08:54.151
<i>She and her...
ambulance-chaser husband tried to sue me.</i>

160
00:08:54.262 --> 00:08:56.355
- So how did you leave things?
- Well. in the end...

161
00:08:56.465 --> 00:08:58.831
it didn't matter what the rest of us thought.

162
00:08:58.934 --> 00:09:01.300
Julie and Jenny were gonna
have to come to an agreement.

163
00:09:01.403 --> 00:09:04.167
I wonder if they thought
they could continue...

164
00:09:04.272 --> 00:09:06.604
<i>to work in the circus if they were separated.</i>

165
00:09:06.708 --> 00:09:09.040
Well. they both loved the circus.

166
00:09:09.144 --> 00:09:11.044
Yeah. Jenny told me once...

167
00:09:11.146 --> 00:09:14.547
that they had some ideas
on how to expand their act.

168
00:09:14.649 --> 00:09:18.710
Sounds likeJenny was the bossy one
and Julie was a little nicer?

169
00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:22.085
Well. they were like any other sisters.

170
00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:26.217
They had distinct
personalities and strengths.

171
00:09:26.328 --> 00:09:29.627
<i>If there's anything else
I can do to help the F.B.I.-</i>

172
00:09:29.731 --> 00:09:31.198
Yeah. Tell you what.

173
00:09:31.299 --> 00:09:32.994
Send the records to the F.B.I.
in Washington.

174
00:09:33.101 --> 00:09:35.695
- Why can't you simply take them with you?
- We have another appointment.

175
00:09:35.804 --> 00:09:37.533
- Thank you for your cooperation.
- Mm-hmm.

176
00:09:42.977 --> 00:09:45.969
The F.B.I. did a wonderful job with this trailer.

177
00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.708
Okay. Just lose the Katharine Hepburn voice.

178
00:09:48.816 --> 00:09:51.683
I'm just trying to find my character.
You know. acting.

179
00:09:51.785 --> 00:09:55.585
Well. don't.
It sounds ridiculous. Okay. Bones?

180
00:09:55.689 --> 00:09:57.680
<i>What's my name there. Wanda?</i>

181
00:09:57.791 --> 00:09:59.986
It's written right there
on the side of the truck...

182
00:10:00.094 --> 00:10:02.085
which "high wire" is not.

183
00:10:02.196 --> 00:10:03.629
It's just sometimes you get irritated...

184
00:10:03.731 --> 00:10:05.198
and you say "Booth" without thinking.

185
00:10:05.299 --> 00:10:08.496
I don't do anything without thinking- ever. Buck.

186
00:10:15.509 --> 00:10:17.841
Buck and Wanda and Their Knives of Death. huh?

187
00:10:17.945 --> 00:10:19.207
Never heard of ya.

188
00:10:19.313 --> 00:10:22.544
We've worked the Pacific Northwest.
Canada. Alaska.

189
00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:25.050
I guess that makes you
the beautiful assistant then?

190
00:10:25.152 --> 00:10:27.552
Wanda. Yes.
I'm also quite adept on the high wire.

191
00:10:27.655 --> 00:10:31.352
Well. I gotta admit it would be nice
to have a knife-throwing act around.

192
00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:33.449
Yeah. well. folks. they love a little danger.

193
00:10:33.561 --> 00:10:36.121
- So what's your thing?
- Our thing?

194
00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:39.791
Yeah. Your gimmick.
You know. a cowboy and Indian princess.

195
00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:42.460
A pirate and kidnapped princess.

196
00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.130
AJack the Ripper and... princess.

197
00:10:45.239 --> 00:10:48.037
- We're Russian.
- Or the "cowboy and Indian princess" thing.

198
00:10:48.142 --> 00:10:50.542
<i>No. no. no. The Russian thing sounds good.</i>

199
00:10:50.644 --> 00:10:52.043
- It does?
- Yeah.

200
00:10:52.146 --> 00:10:53.943
- Yeah. Okay. yeah. We are "Ruska. "
- All right.

201
00:10:54.048 --> 00:10:56.016
Well. you do the first show for free...

202
00:10:56.116 --> 00:10:58.277
and. if I like you. then we talk payment.

203
00:11:02.389 --> 00:11:03.913
Wow.

204
00:11:05.392 --> 00:11:07.622
Uh. you-you ain't seen nothin' yet.

205
00:11:07.728 --> 00:11:10.389
Lavalle!

206
00:11:10.496 --> 00:11:12.657
You two ain't the first of May. are you?

207
00:11:12.765 --> 00:11:17.327
- No. In fact. we are not-
- We are no first of May.

208
00:11:17.437 --> 00:11:19.905
This is Lavalle. He's our 24-hour man.

209
00:11:20.006 --> 00:11:23.237
Lavalle. meet Buck and Wanda Moosejaw.
They do a barber act.

210
00:11:23.343 --> 00:11:26.904
- Moosejaw? What are you- Indian?
- Canadian.

211
00:11:27.013 --> 00:11:30.073
<i>Lavalle will show you where to park
your digs. You can get ready for the show.</i>

212
00:11:30.183 --> 00:11:32.481
- They any good?
- How about that?

213
00:11:32.585 --> 00:11:35.247
<i>Hell. being able to splinter a post
don't make you a showman.</i>

214
00:11:35.355 --> 00:11:38.984
We're show people. all right.
You will be amazed.

215
00:11:39.092 --> 00:11:41.424
Ha!

216
00:11:46.232 --> 00:11:48.200
Russian? You had to pick Russian?

217
00:11:48.301 --> 00:11:50.701
<i>Brilliant. right? It just popped into my head.</i>

218
00:11:50.803 --> 00:11:53.636
Well. you know what? Don't pop things. Bones.

219
00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:56.334
- Sweets. what the hell is "the first of May?"
- A newbie.

220
00:11:56.442 --> 00:11:58.376
A rookie.

221
00:11:58.478 --> 00:12:01.208
Why would a little person
be referred to as a 24-hour man?

222
00:12:01.314 --> 00:12:03.305
Oh. Having a little trouble
with the lingo. huh?

223
00:12:03.416 --> 00:12:05.008
He is the advance person.

224
00:12:05.118 --> 00:12:08.110
He goes to town ahead of the circus
and sets everything up.

225
00:12:08.221 --> 00:12:11.281
