00:24:01.625 --> 00:24:03.217
Scenario number three.

446
00:24:03.327 --> 00:24:05.227
They're assaulted separately by a weapon.

447
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.695
That's possible.

448
00:24:10.801 --> 00:24:13.929
- Oh. no. Actually. it's not.
- Why not?

449
00:24:14.038 --> 00:24:16.666
Well. because the wounds are
absolutely symmetrical here.

450
00:24:16.774 --> 00:24:19.572
The possibility of an assailant
striking them separately...

451
00:24:19.677 --> 00:24:23.135
at the exact same angle.
with the exact same force- it ain't gonna happen.

452
00:24:23.247 --> 00:24:27.343
<i>Okay. Well. the heads
could've been conked together.</i>

453
00:24:29.185 --> 00:24:31.380
<i>There'd be evidence
on the soft tissue of the face.</i>

454
00:24:31.488 --> 00:24:33.353
No. There was no soft tissue left.

455
00:24:33.456 --> 00:24:37.222
What if the blunt instrument was soft?

456
00:24:37.327 --> 00:24:39.921
What. like a pillow?

457
00:24:40.030 --> 00:24:42.089
Oh. wait a second.

458
00:24:42.198 --> 00:24:45.099
Clown props.

459
00:24:45.201 --> 00:24:48.693
- I'll call Booth and Dr. Brennan.
- Nice.

460
00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:52.975
When Cortez conquered the Aztecs...

461
00:24:53.076 --> 00:24:54.976
clowns were among the many treasures...

462
00:24:55.078 --> 00:24:57.740
he carried back to Clement VII.

463
00:24:57.847 --> 00:25:00.372
Thank you. That's-

464
00:25:03.753 --> 00:25:05.812
Ah!

465
00:25:05.922 --> 00:25:08.152
- You ready?
- Yes.

466
00:25:08.258 --> 00:25:10.988
Ready to throw knives at beautiful woman.

467
00:25:11.094 --> 00:25:13.927
- Not "at." I hope.
- Right. No. of course.

468
00:25:14.030 --> 00:25:16.191
Ha-ha. Around.

469
00:25:16.299 --> 00:25:19.894
Wow! Wanda. You-You look-

470
00:25:20.003 --> 00:25:22.528
- Wow.
- You too. uh. Boris.

471
00:25:22.639 --> 00:25:25.073
You make beautiful Natasha.

472
00:25:25.175 --> 00:25:27.507
Man. you act like
this is the first time you've done this.

473
00:25:27.610 --> 00:25:31.410
- Yeah. well. we like to keep things fresh.
- So I've seen.

474
00:25:31.514 --> 00:25:33.812
Okay. So. um-

475
00:25:33.917 --> 00:25:37.216
I stand against a board. right.
with balloons all around me...

476
00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:40.255
and then you pop them
with your razor-sharp knives?

477
00:25:40.356 --> 00:25:44.190
Right. Unless we do our actual job
and find the murder weapon.

478
00:25:44.294 --> 00:25:47.195
- What's with the mustache?
- I thought it would add a nice Russian flair.

479
00:25:47.297 --> 00:25:50.789
- It looks like a small animal.
- Too short.

480
00:25:50.900 --> 00:25:54.836
There's a giant plastic ice-cream cone.
a giant plastic shoe...

481
00:25:54.938 --> 00:25:58.532
a giant plastic phone. a giant plastic-

482
00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:01.268
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa!

483
00:26:01.376 --> 00:26:03.344
Mind telling me what you're doing here?

484
00:26:03.445 --> 00:26:06.312
Oh. what. you gonna play tough?
You're clowns. right?

485
00:26:06.415 --> 00:26:09.782
- I throw knives.
- Let's kick his ass.

486
00:26:09.885 --> 00:26:13.821
- Yeah. bring it on. Bozo.
- Uh. we're just looking for a prop. That's all.

487
00:26:13.922 --> 00:26:18.120
<i>Buck here is going to knock
this nose off my face with a knife.</i>

488
00:26:18.227 --> 00:26:21.993
Why does everyone think the clown stuff
is there for everyone?

489
00:26:22.097 --> 00:26:24.964
<i>- This is our stuff.
- Let's kick his ass. you guys.</i>

490
00:26:25.067 --> 00:26:28.264
<i>Traditionally.
clowns are fun loving and anarchistic.</i>

491
00:26:28.370 --> 00:26:32.136
- You are rigid and humorless.
- Let's kick both their asses!

492
00:26:32.241 --> 00:26:34.641
You better have your biggest
ass-kicking shoes on.

493
00:26:34.743 --> 00:26:36.836
Stop!

494
00:26:38.347 --> 00:26:40.679
If y'all want to have a Clem.
that's your business.

495
00:26:40.782 --> 00:26:42.909
But after the show.

496
00:26:46.288 --> 00:26:50.452
- Tumbles. I'm serious.
- Your call.

497
00:26:50.559 --> 00:26:53.858
- All right. Let's go. guys.
- Not so funny now. eh. Tumbles?

498
00:26:55.264 --> 00:26:57.164
That's enough. Moosejaw.

499
00:26:57.266 --> 00:27:00.963
We're lining up.
You two damn well better be ready.

500
00:27:01.069 --> 00:27:04.368
- Thinks he's so big.
- I'm ready. How about you?

501
00:27:04.473 --> 00:27:07.738
- Yeah. I'm ready. Oh. God. Bones.
- Oh! My eye.

502
00:27:07.843 --> 00:27:09.970
- You okay?
- I'm okay.

503
00:27:10.078 --> 00:27:12.376
Well. we can't do the show now.

504
00:27:12.481 --> 00:27:15.712
What? No. The show must go on.

505
00:27:17.019 --> 00:27:18.577
Says who?

506
00:27:21.323 --> 00:27:25.850
<i>Ladies and gentlemen and children of all ages...</i>

507
00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:28.758
welcome to Bingham's Circus of Wonders...

508
00:27:28.863 --> 00:27:31.593
<i>the most sensational. death-defying...</i>

509
00:27:31.699 --> 00:27:35.260
one-ring spectacular on earth!

510
00:27:37.572 --> 00:27:41.201
<i>Here they come! Yea!</i>

511
00:27:44.579 --> 00:27:46.547
Hoo. hoo-hoo-hoo!

512
00:27:50.585 --> 00:27:52.280
<i>Hello. hello!</i>

513
00:27:54.055 --> 00:27:55.579
<i>Hey. hey!</i>

514
00:27:58.893 --> 00:28:02.124
<i>Good day! Good day!</i>

515
00:28:05.166 --> 00:28:07.100
They're clapping for us.

516
00:28:07.201 --> 00:28:09.601
Smile. Boris. and wave.

517
00:28:09.704 --> 00:28:12.332
Show them your knives. Come on.

518
00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:14.271
Where's the Buck Moosejaw I married?

519
00:28:24.185 --> 00:28:26.585
