a lot more than that.

527
00:28:46.040 --> 00:28:49.635
There is no act. remember?
There's just me trying not to kill you.

528
00:28:49.744 --> 00:28:53.271
You said you were very good-
trained in knife skills by the military.

529
00:28:53.381 --> 00:28:56.440
Oh. I am very good.
but it's you I am concerned for.

530
00:28:56.549 --> 00:29:00.280
Well. if you say you're skilled. then I have
no reason to doubt you. do I?

531
00:29:00.387 --> 00:29:04.221
You know. it's not good
for the barbers to fight before a show.

532
00:29:05.392 --> 00:29:07.553
Those things are sharp.

533
00:29:07.661 --> 00:29:11.153
Let's just get through this.
all right. Mrs. Moosejaw?

534
00:29:11.264 --> 00:29:12.993
Okay.

535
00:29:15.402 --> 00:29:17.495
Look at that.

536
00:29:17.604 --> 00:29:20.232
The clowns are using those fake barbells.

537
00:29:23.710 --> 00:29:25.678
<i>One of them could've clocked the twins...</i>

538
00:29:25.779 --> 00:29:27.679
and smashed their heads together.

539
00:29:27.781 --> 00:29:30.147
The bar joining the foam weights together.
it's too short.

540
00:29:30.250 --> 00:29:34.277
The fulcrum wouldn't give any of them
sufficient force to cause a kissing fracture.

541
00:29:34.387 --> 00:29:36.912
They're clowns. They have their ways.

542
00:29:37.023 --> 00:29:39.287
<i>Folks. thanks a lot. See you later on.</i>

543
00:29:39.392 --> 00:29:41.883
<i>- You're up.
- And now...</i>

544
00:29:41.995 --> 00:29:46.557
<i>direct from their triumphant tour
of Europe and the Far East...</i>

545
00:29:46.666 --> 00:29:51.729
<i>Bingham's Circus of Wonders
is proud to present the razor-sharp skills...</i>

546
00:29:51.838 --> 00:29:54.898
of the most thrilling.
the most breathtaking...

547
00:29:55.008 --> 00:29:59.035
<i>the most dangerous
knife-throwing act in the world.</i>

548
00:29:59.145 --> 00:30:03.309
Boris and Natasha
and Their Russian Knives of Death!

549
00:30:11.524 --> 00:30:15.119
- Huh. What's up with Brennan's eye?
- Eye patch. That's very rakish.

550
00:30:15.228 --> 00:30:17.355
Plus. she only has to be half as scared.

551
00:30:19.466 --> 00:30:23.868
Bones. just keep your arms
outstretched like this. okay?

552
00:30:23.969 --> 00:30:26.028
- Be very. very still.
- Okay.

553
00:30:26.138 --> 00:30:29.733
- Shouldn't the balloons be closer to my body?
- Not if you want to live.

554
00:30:41.653 --> 00:30:43.484
Waah!

555
00:31:07.079 --> 00:31:10.537
<i>That was amazing! That was really amazing!</i>

556
00:31:36.141 --> 00:31:38.268
- Oh!
- Whoo!

557
00:31:40.546 --> 00:31:44.141
<i>Da! Da!</i>

558
00:31:44.249 --> 00:31:46.717
<i>Natasha's balloons are no match...</i>

559
00:31:46.819 --> 00:31:50.812
for Boris's Knives of Death!

560
00:31:50.923 --> 00:31:55.188
<i>Ah! Da! Hmm.</i>

561
00:31:57.028 --> 00:31:59.826
- Ah!
- Hmm?

562
00:32:03.434 --> 00:32:08.667
<i>Boris. Moya lyubov.
Spare the life of your lyubov.</i>

563
00:32:11.642 --> 00:32:13.371
<i>Da.</i>

564
00:32:16.447 --> 00:32:18.915
<i>Definitely. Da.</i>

565
00:32:20.318 --> 00:32:23.014
Are they sure they know what they're doing?

566
00:32:35.867 --> 00:32:38.267
<i>Oh!</i>

567
00:32:38.369 --> 00:32:41.668
Hey!

568
00:32:41.772 --> 00:32:44.366
You really are as good as you said.
You should try a blindfold.

569
00:32:44.475 --> 00:32:46.443
Says the half-blind woman.

570
00:32:59.824 --> 00:33:02.452
<i>Is it me. or does she seem
a little too into this?</i>

571
00:33:02.560 --> 00:33:05.358
Well. there is. of course.
a sexual component to an act of this sort.

572
00:33:05.463 --> 00:33:07.226
- The knife representing-
- We get it.

573
00:33:07.331 --> 00:33:11.199
Dr. Brennan is showing
remarkable trust and willingness.

574
00:33:11.302 --> 00:33:13.202
<i>Be careful!</i>

575
00:33:13.304 --> 00:33:15.238
<i>She's only got one eye left!</i>

576
00:33:15.339 --> 00:33:18.240
<i>Da! Da!</i>

577
00:33:59.115 --> 00:34:02.482
<i>Well. how about that!
Let's hear it for 'em. folks.</i>

578
00:34:02.586 --> 00:34:07.046
<i>Boris the Brave
and the knee-knockingly lovely Natasha!</i>

579
00:34:07.157 --> 00:34:09.625
<i>Come. Boris.</i>

580
00:34:12.062 --> 00:34:14.292
<i>Let 'em hear it. folks.</i>

581
00:34:14.397 --> 00:34:17.127
They loved us. You were great.

582
00:34:17.233 --> 00:34:20.031
Superb hand-eye coordination there.
Buckie.

583
00:34:20.136 --> 00:34:24.698
- I could've killed you.
- Therein lies the excitement for the spectators.

584
00:34:24.808 --> 00:34:30.508
<i>Our own superstrong Mighty Magnum!</i>

585
00:34:30.614 --> 00:34:32.172
<i>- My God.
- What?</i>

586
00:34:32.282 --> 00:34:35.183
Magnum. Look.

587
00:34:38.822 --> 00:34:41.950
He definitely has the upper-body strength
to swing a foam barbell...

588
00:34:42.058 --> 00:34:44.288
<i>hard enough to cause those fractures.</i>

589
00:34:44.394 --> 00:34:46.726
<i>Check out those arms of steel!</i>

590
00:34:49.099 --> 00:34:53.296
<i>- Hey there. big guy. You got a minute?
- For what?</i>

591
00:34:53.402 --> 00:34:56.894
I want to ask you a question
about my friends. Julie and Jenny.

592
00:34:57.006 --> 00:35:00.464
Look. this is getting old. Now. I told you.

593
00:35:00.576 --> 00:35:04.205
They were here. They left. That's all I know.
Check with some other circuses maybe.

594
00:35:04.313 --> 00:35:07.282
- They're dead. But you knew that. didn't you?
- Dead?

595
00:35:07.383 --> 00:35:11.820
- What are you talking about?
- Their heads were smashed together. weren't they?

596
00:35:16.859 --> 00:35:19.054
- Oh!
- Oh! Geez.

597
00:35:19.161 --> 00:35:22.221
- That guy is strong.
- Well. he is called a "strong man. "

598
00:35:22.331 --> 00:35:25.630
- Well. help me get out of this.
- I'm trying to get out.

599
00:35:29.338 --> 00:35:31.932
<i>Look. I want to put
a BOLO on this guy right away.</i>

600
00:35:32.041 --> 00:35:36.137
Magnum the Strong Man.
Real name- Norman von Gluck.

601
00:35:36.245 --> 00:35:39.271
Well. of course he's big.
He's a strong man.

602
00:35:39.381 --> 00:35:41.349
Look. he's wearing a tank top
that says "Magnum. "

603
00:35:41.450 --> 00:35:43.418
He shouldn't be too hard to spot.

604
00:35:43.519 --> 00:35:46.784
Mr. Nigel-Murray has found
some additional bone anomalies.

605
00:35:46.889 --> 00:35:50.757
<i>- Can you explain?
- "Anomaly." from the Greek anomalos.</i>

606
00:35:50.859 --> 00:35:53.953
I'm thinking we could move
this along a bit faster. Mr. Nigel-Murray.

607
00:35:54.063 --> 00:35:57.726
I found slight longitudinal fractures...

608
00:35:57.833 --> 00:36:00.961
along the distal ends
of all four lower leg bones...

609
00:36:01.070 --> 00:36:03.038
and stress fractures on the cuboids.

610
00:36:03.138 --> 00:36:05.800
Fractures to the lower legs and feet.

611
00:36:05.908 --> 00:36:08.741
Does the guy torture 'em first?
Rubber hose to the feet?

612
00:36:08.844 --> 00:36:12.143
<i>That wouldn't be consistent with the injuries
which are isolated to those specific areas.</i>

613
00:36:12.247 --> 00:36:14.215
<i>Can you send me the X-rays?</i>

614
00:36:14.316 --> 00:36:16.284
- The X-rays are-
- They're on their way.

615
00:36:16.385 --> 00:36:18.284
I was more than capable of telling her that.

616
00:36:18.386 --> 00:36:21.253
I was afraid you'd start talking
about Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen...

617
00:36:21.355 --> 00:36:22.947
and the discovery of the X-ray.

618
00:36:23.057 --> 00:36:26.458
November the 8th. 1895.
He made an image of his wife's hand-

619
00:36:26.561 --> 00:36:30.156
I rest my case.
By the way. we all loved your show.

620
00:36:30.264 --> 00:36:32.425
Oh. thank you. Did you hear the cheering?

621
00:36:32.533 --> 00:36:35.058
- Eh. it was all for me.
- Booth was undeniably good.

622
00:36:35.169 --> 00:36:38.229
<i>However. he's not very imaginative
as far as the act goes.</i>

623
00:36:38.339 --> 00:36:42.275
<i>Look. there is a difference
between imagination and tempting fate.</i>

624
00:36:42.376 --> 00:36:44.571
I am just asking for a little flair.

625
00:36:44.679 --> 00:36:46.647
Flair? You want flair-

626
00:36:46.748 --> 00:36:49.410
- Can I ask about the eye?
- No.

627
00:36:49.517 --> 00:36:52.247
<i>I was thinking
that I could wear a hat of fruit...</i>

628
00:36:52.353 --> 00:36:54.913
and then you could slice
through each fruit while-

629
00:36:55.022 --> 00:36:57.582
Bones. it's over. No more undercover.

630
00:36:57.692 --> 00:37:00.593
The act. it's over.

631
00:37:03.698 --> 00:37:07.828
We have to go question the other performers.

632
00:37:07.935 --> 00:37:09.903
Right.

633
00:37:11.239 --> 00:37:13.707
Hey.

634
00:37:13.808 --> 00:37:16.106
You two want to explain
what happened with Magnum?

635
00:37:16.210 --> 00:37:18.303
- He trapped us in the net.
- For no reason?

636
00:37:18.412 --> 00:37:20.471
- We asked him about the twins.
- Asked what?

637
00:37:20.581 --> 00:37:23.015
<i>Ifhe knew anything about how they died.</i>

638
00:37:26.387 --> 00:37:28.685
<i>- You want us to take care of this?
- Settle.</i>

639
00:37:28.790 --> 00:37:31.350
- Who are you people?
- F.B.I. Special Agent Seeley Booth.

640
00:37:31.459 --> 00:37:34.951
<i>And Dr. Temperance Brennan
of theJeffersonian Institution.</i>

641
00:37:35.062 --> 00:37:37.030
Okay. uh.
the Van Owen twins were murdered.

642
00:37:37.131 --> 00:37:39.292
Our prime suspect right now is Magnum.

643
00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:41.391
He had the requisite strength.

644
00:37:41.502 --> 00:37:45.700
- Magnum never killed anyone.
- People. can you please come back now?

645
00:37:45.807 --> 00:37:47.967
- Tell them to come back.
- None of us are gonna help you.

646
00:37:48.074 --> 00:37:52.067
- Don't you care what happened to the twins?
- You aren't one of us.

647
00:37:52.179 --> 00:37:55.410
You don't get it. do you?
How could you? You're gillies.

648
00:37:55.515 --> 00:37:58.712
No. No. We're not gillies. Our act was good.

649
00:37:58.819 --> 00:38:01.515
Yeah. You're gillies.

650
00:38:03.390 --> 00:38:06.086
- Right.
- We have no case.

651
00:38:06.193 --> 00:38:08.093
Yeah. We will when we bring Magnum in.

652
00:38:08.195 --> 00:38:12.029
We have no definitive forensics
tying him or anyone else to the murder.

653
00:38:12.132 --> 00:38:14.600
You will when you get back to the lab.
You'll find evidence.

654
00:38:14.701 --> 00:38:18.535
The "boneus maximus"
will have his initials on it or something.

655
00:38:20.807 --> 00:38:24.675
<i>I really was pretty good on the high wire.</i>

656
00:38:25.846 --> 00:38:29.282
- I'm gonna try it.
- No- Up there? Now?

657
00:38:29.382 --> 00:38:32.180
Wait a second. Bones. no.
You will-You'll fall. It's too high.

658
00:38:32.285 --> 00:38:35.448
- There's a net.
- You got no depth perception. You have a patch on your eye.

659
00:38:35.555 --> 00:38:38.888
- You won't be able to see.
- No. It's more a case of feel.

660
00:38:38.992 --> 00:38:41.392
- I could do it with my eyes shut.
- You shut your eyes...

661
00:38:41.494 --> 00:38:43.462
and I will shut mine.
'cause I am not watching.

662
00:38:43.563 --> 00:38:46.191
My teacher said I was
one of his best students.

663
00:38:48.568 --> 00:38:50.627
This is crazy.

664
00:38:56.710 --> 00:38:59.304
<i>- Booth. look!
- No.</i>

665
00:38:59.412 --> 00:39:02.108
I told you. I'm not gonna look.
I'm keeping my eyes shut.

666
00:39:02.215 --> 00:39:05.275
<i>This is absolutely- Oh. my God.</i>

667
00:39:05.385 --> 00:39:08.616
<i>Bones. Whoo! Wow! You are fearless.</i>

668
00:39:10.523 --> 00:39:12.491
My feet. I'm not in shape for this.

669
00:39:12.592 --> 00:39:14.787
<i>Look at you. You're doing great.</i>

670
00:39:14.895 --> 00:39:17.124
You think maybe you
could ride a bike on that thing...

671
00:39:17.229 --> 00:39:19.493
and maybe spin a ball on your nose
at the same time?

672
00:39:19.598 --> 00:39:21.759
<i>- Ow! My cuboids.
- Your what?</i>

673
00:39:21.867 --> 00:39:25.598
- The cuboids are the bones in my feet.
- Bones. you all right?

674
00:39:27.072 --> 00:39:30.803
- Bones.
- Yeah. I'm fine.

675
00:39:30.910 --> 00:39:33.276
<i>Oh. my God!</i>

676
00:39:33.379 --> 00:39:36.314
<i>Bones. are you all right?</i>

677
00:39:36.415 --> 00:39:39.782
<i>Yeah. I'm fine.
I know what happened.</i>

678
00:39:39.885 --> 00:39:43.184
- It's pretty obvious. You lost your balance.
- No. To the twins.

679
00:39:43.289 --> 00:39:45.780
They weren't murdered.

680
00:39:45.891 --> 00:39:48.758
<i>The stress fractures
to their fibulas and cuboids?</i>

681
00:39:48.861 --> 00:39:51.295
They were caused by walking on the high wire.

682
00:39:51.397 --> 00:39:53.695
And-And the kissing fracture?

683
00:39:53.799 --> 00:39:56.097
Their heads snapped together
when they fell into the net.

684
00:39:56.201 --> 00:39:58.169
<i>That's why there was no other trauma.</i>

685
00:39:58.270 --> 00:40:00.830
Oh. A conjoined twin high wire act.

686
00:40:00.940 --> 00:40:03.465
Henry said thatJenny wanted to be famous.

687
00:40:03.575 --> 00:40:06.043
Their act would've been completely unique.

688
00:40:10.416 --> 00:40:12.384
<i>Well. that's a first.</i>

689
00:40:12.484 --> 00:40:15.476
Yeah. He covered up an accident
by making it look like a murder.

690
00:40:15.587 --> 00:40:18.283
<i>I didn't kill 'em.</i>

691
00:40:18.390 --> 00:40:20.483
I didn't kill 'em.

692
00:40:21.527 --> 00:40:23.495
I loved them.

693
00:40:23.595 --> 00:40:26.029
- I would never hurt them.
- We know.

694
00:40:26.131 --> 00:40:29.862
<i>I buried them.
and they needed a proper burial.</i>

695
00:40:31.637 --> 00:40:33.730
Don't say anything. Magnum.

696
00:40:33.839 --> 00:40:37.172
<i>You asked them not to go on the high wire.
but that's exactly what they wanted to do.</i>

697
00:40:37.276 --> 00:40:39.904
It's probably the only thing
Julie and Jenny ever agreed on.

698
00:40:40.012 --> 00:40:43.743
When they dropped to the net. the force
of the fall snapped their heads together.

699
00:40:43.849 --> 00:40:46.783
<i>An accident like that.
their mother definitely would've sued.</i>

700
00:40:46.884 --> 00:40:48.852
The circus would never have survived.

701
00:40:50.588 --> 00:40:53.716
I'm gonna have to arrest you
for interference with a dead body.

702
00:40:53.825 --> 00:40:57.158
- We're sorry. Aren't we?
- Yeah.

703
00:40:57.261 --> 00:41:00.526
- Sorry.
- We're going to get you a good lawyer.

704
00:41:00.631 --> 00:41:02.997
Just don't bring them into this.

705
00:41:03.101 --> 00:41:06.434
'Cause I don't wanna see
the circus die because of me.

706
00:41:06.537 --> 00:41:09.028
<i>What you're gonna have to explain
is why you wrapped 'em in a sheet...</i>

707
00:41:09.140 --> 00:41:12.576
<i>because that's something a woman
would do out of respect.</i>

708
00:41:12.677 --> 00:41:16.670
You'll also have to explain
how you forged their handwriting on a note.

709
00:41:19.217 --> 00:41:22.209
Yeah. I will.

710
00:41:23.588 --> 00:41:25.283
Thanks.

711
00:41:31.963 --> 00:41:36.263
<i>Well. I'll just call up the Dallas field office
and have them pick him up.</i>

712
00:41:36.367 --> 00:41:38.358
<i>Think he'll run again?</i>

713
00:41:40.471 --> 00:41:42.200
<i>No. He won't run.</i>

714
00:41:42.306 --> 00:41:45.366
<i>#Some are reaching. Few are there #</i>

715
00:41:48.112 --> 00:41:52.173
<i># Want to reign from a hero's chair#</i>

716
00:41:55.486 --> 00:41:59.354
<i># Some are scared to fly so high #</i>

717
00:42:01.492 --> 00:42:05.189
<i># Well. this is how we have to try #</i>

718
00:42:05.296 --> 00:42:09.096
<i># Have no envy and no fear#</i>

719
00:42:09.200 --> 00:42:11.464
<i># Have no envy #</i>

720
00:42:12.904 --> 00:42:14.928
<i># And no fear#</i>

721
00:42:19.409 --> 00:42:22.105
- They're gone.
- Yeah.

722
00:42:22.212 --> 00:42:24.544
- We slept through it?
- Yeah. Yeah.

723
00:42:24.648 --> 00:42:28.607
"Boris and Natasha
and Their Russian Knives of Death. "

724
00:42:28.718 --> 00:42:30.686
I guess we all got it in us. huh?

725
00:42:30.787 --> 00:42:33.779
The desire to run off and join the circus.

726
00:42:36.326 --> 00:42:39.489
